XOTAR

**Local cognitive shell for Ollama** — watch the model think between turns.

Single-file research prototype: global workspace, sleep-time consolidation, prediction-error loop, initiative/murmur, and an honest capability scorecard.

> Not a second-brain note app. Not a memory API for other agents.  
> A self-contained cognitive loop you can open in the browser.

---

## What you get

- **Global workspace** — limited attention slots + saliency
- **Memory consolidation** — decay, replay, synthesis (similarity-based)
- **Dream cycle** — bridges, open questions, dream journal while idle
- **Murmur & initiative** — quiet inner notes and follow-ups when you leave the tab
- **Prediction-error loop** — generate expectations, score them later
- **Structured actions** — human-in-the-loop whitelist
- **Butlin-style scorecard** — explicit `yes` / `part` / `no` (no hype claims)
- **Graph UI** — Cytoscape view of concepts and links
- **100% local** — Ollama + browser; data stays on your machine

---

## Quick start

1. Install [Ollama](https://ollama.com) and pull a model, e.g.  
   `ollama pull llama3.2`
2. Enable CORS for the browser (example):  
   `OLLAMA_ORIGINS="*"` when starting Ollama (see Ollama docs for your OS)
3. Open `Xotar.html` (or the latest release file) in Chrome/Firefox
4. Point the app at `http://localhost:11434` and chat

No account. No cloud. No build step.

---

## What this is / isn’t

| Is | Isn’t |
|----|--------|
| Research / portfolio prototype | Production multi-user SaaS |
| Cognitive architecture experiment | Obsidian replacement or Khoj clone |
| Visible thinking (graph + scorecard) | Black-box memory API (Mem0-style) |
| Single HTML file on purpose | Claim of machine consciousness |

The scorecard is intentionally conservative. Gaps are marked `part` or `no`.

---

## Architecture (short)
Chat / idle

→ retrieve + workspace

→ persona prompt (+ temporal context)

→ Ollama

→ consolidate / dream / predict / maybe initiate

→ graph + scorecard updateText
Persistence: `localStorage` / IndexedDB in the browser. Export/import JSON supported in-app.

---

